# d-flash2-checkpoint-watch
owner: d-flash-benchmarker · cadence: every morning · status: SUGGESTED
**I see the checkpoint-before-experiment rule keeps needing enforcement and the 81 tok/s save was never confirmed — want a loop that checks the current fast build still has a valid checkpoint before you move on?**

## Prompt
Check whether the current fast build in faster-without has a current checkpoint; if not, flag it so the fix-tables-then-checkpoint ordering is honored before any DFlash2 move.

## Evidence
> "before you do that save this 81 tokens a second build because that is excellent. I don't want to lose this Save this as a checkpoint"
